+# MASTER HANDOVER — ChallengeEngineV01_STATELESS — C11-C 2.16.9 FROZEN
+
+## Authoritative baseline
+
+The **sole authoritative baseline for the next context** is the Library file:
+
+`ChallengeEngine-C11-C2.16.9 FROZEN.zip`
+
+When continuing in another context, retrieve this exact Library file before making assumptions about the current source tree. Do not silently reconstruct the state from older C11-C ZIPs, summaries or superseded handovers when the frozen archive is available.
+
+## Frozen milestone
+
+C11-C 2.16 is frozen as the stable manufacturing milestone for Visual Loops, Visual Drills and the shared C11-C production/review system.
+
+The completed audiovisual review corpus is:
+
+- 27 Visual Loop grammars;
+- 5 Visual Loop families;
+- 20 Visual Drill review renders;
+- 4 Visual Drill families;
+- 5 family Longforms of 180 seconds.
+
+Total review corpus: **52 audiovisual contents**.
+
+## Frozen boundaries
+
+Do not reopen or alter without a new explicit checkpoint, contract revision and regression evidence:
+
+- C11-B simulation truth;
+- challenge runtime truth and certified mechanics;
+- structural RNG ownership;
+- `SimulationResult`;
+- `winning_frame`;
+- `close_calls`;
+- `WinningFrameDetector`;
+- `RenderedFrameStream` semantics;
+- C7 audio ownership/contracts;
+- C9 challenge authoring semantics;
+- logical 540×960 social geometry.
+
+Presentation and orchestration may consume these contracts but must not manufacture gameplay truth.
+
+## Current C11-C manufacturing facts
+
+- Physical review output: 720×1280 / 30 FPS.
+- Visual Loops: 20–23 seconds.
+- Visual Drills: Tracking 27 seconds total; Saccade/Pursuit/Peripheral Scan 23 seconds total.
+- Longforms: 180 seconds.
+- Header: 3-line capacity, Inter Bold, shared Matrix metric.
+- Footer: up to 3 lines, Noto Sans Mono.
+- Separators visible.
+- AVI temporary by default; GIF opt-in.
+- Review tooling: 7 workers and resumable state.
+
+## Current next phase
+
+Complete the transition from art-direction manufacturing to the original **Video Challenger + Asset Recovery** problem.
+
+The order is deliberate:
+
+1. consolidate current documentation;
+2. audit Meta/Reels delivery without reopening the frozen C11-C master;
+3. finish and operationalize `c11c-producer` as the single UI orchestration surface;
+4. recover and catalogue the original challenge corpus and real assets;
+5. only then implement the next challenge generation work.
+
+## Producer principle
+
+`c11c-producer` is an orchestration/UI layer. It must not copy mechanics, RNG, simulation calculations or renderer logic into Python.
+
+The GUI must preserve its existing two-column light interface and extend it instead of replacing it.
+
+## Historical documentation rule
+
+Never rewrite a historical checkpoint so that it falsely describes later functionality. Historical documents remain under `docs/history/` and are interpreted through the audit/index. Current truth is under `docs/current/`.
